### 2. src/indexer.rs

In `EventIndexer::initialize()`, when both `state.inbox_last_block` and `state.outbox_last_block` are `Some`, the code already fetches `inbox_ts`/`outbox_ts` for them to decide `needs_init`. Reuse those same already-fetched values as true lower bounds: if `inbox_ts < indexing_since`, then `inbox_b` (the old last-synced block) is provably <= the answer for a search targeting `indexing_since` (same monotonicity argument), so seed with it; same for outbox. When either side is `None` (first-ever run, nothing to seed from), that side's lo stays 0 — there is no prior state to derive a true lower bound from, and 0 is the correct, safe fallback (don't try to invent a finalized-block floor here — `indexing_since` is typically many days in the past, so a finalized/near-head block would basically never satisfy `<= indexing_since`; not worth the extra RPC call and complexity for near-zero benefit).

Restructure roughly like:

```rust
pub async fn initialize(&self) {
    self.task_store.lock().unwrap().set_on_sync(false);
    let state = self.task_store.lock().unwrap().load();

    let inbox_now = self.route.inbox_provider.get_block_by_number(Default::default()).await
        .expect("Failed to get inbox block")
        .expect("Inbox block not found")
        .header.timestamp;

    let indexing_since = inbox_now.saturating_sub(self.route.settings.sync_lookback_secs);

    let mut inbox_lo = 0;
    let mut outbox_lo = 0;
    let needs_init = match (state.inbox_last_block, state.outbox_last_block) {
        (None, _) | (_, None) => true,
        (Some(inbox_b), Some(outbox_b)) => {
            let inbox_ts = self.route.inbox_provider.get_block_by_number(inbox_b.into()).await
                .expect("Failed to get inbox last block")
                .expect("Inbox last block not found")
                .header.timestamp;
            let outbox_ts = self.route.outbox_provider.get_block_by_number(outbox_b.into()).await
                .expect("Failed to get outbox last block")
                .expect("Outbox last block not found")
                .header.timestamp;

            // A previously synced block whose timestamp already precedes the new
            // `indexing_since` cutoff is a true lower bound for the re-seeded search:
            // real scanning already covered up to it, so the answer can't be before it.
            if inbox_ts < indexing_since {
                inbox_lo = inbox_b;
            }
            if outbox_ts < indexing_since {
                outbox_lo = outbox_b;
            }

            inbox_ts < indexing_since || outbox_ts < indexing_since
        }
    };

    if needs_init {
        let inbox_start = find_block_by_timestamp_from(&self.route.inbox_provider, indexing_since, inbox_lo).await;
        let outbox_start = find_block_by_timestamp_from(&self.route.outbox_provider, indexing_since, outbox_lo).await;
        self.task_store.lock().unwrap().initialize_sync(indexing_since, inbox_start, outbox_start);
        info!(logger = "Indexer", route = self.route.name, indexing_since, inbox_start, outbox_start, "Initialized sync");
    }
}
```

